### Onboarding: handle. Both calls need a signed-in user.
### Get a token by signing in (see auth.http) and paste its accessToken here:
@token = <paste accessToken>

### Is a handle free? -> { available, suggestions[] }. Rule breakers are just available:false.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/handles/check?handle=pivotmaster
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Taken, reserved or lookalike -> available:false plus 3 free suggestions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/handles/check?handle=ad.min
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Claim a handle -> { handle }
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/handle
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "pivotmaster" }

### 400 HANDLE_INVALID (too short)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/handle
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "ab" }

### 400 HANDLE_RESERVED (a lookalike of "admin")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/handle
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "adm1n" }

### 409 HANDLE_TAKEN: claim a handle another account already holds, in any case
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/handle
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "PIVOTMASTER" }

### 401 without a token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/handles/check?handle=pivotmaster
